/**
* APEX RULES
*/

RULE = Always create a test class alongside each implementation class with more than 75 test cobverage
RULE = Always Generate the meta.xml files for Apex class and Test Class
RULE = Always use the latest API version for any new class created
RULE = Follow OOPS concepts wherever possible
RULE = Follow the DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself) principle across all code
RULE = Implement proper error handling and logging across all layers
RULE = Implement one trigger per object
RULE = Every Apex method used in LWC must have @AuraEnabled annotation
RULE = Escape all user inputs in SOQL queries using String.escapeSingleQuotes()
RULE = Always use a list/map to store query results

// SOQL rules
RULE = Never use Long Text Area fields in SOQL query filters
RULE = Limit query results when appropriate
RULE = Strictly avoid SOQL queries within for loops or any iterative structure

// Testing
RULE = Use @TestSetup for creating test data
RULE = Use Assert class and its methods for assertion
RULE = Always do positive and negative testing
RULE = Consider using ApexMocks for advanced mocking needs

// Design Patterns
FOLLOW_PATTERN = Use the Trigger Handler pattern with one trigger per object that calls a handler class
FOLLOW_PATTERN = Implement Service Layer pattern to separate business logic from data access
FOLLOW_PATTERN = Use Selector Layer pattern for complex SOQL queries
FOLLOW_PATTERN = Follow Factory pattern for creating test data in unit tests
FOLLOW_PATTERN = Implement Singleton pattern for utility classes that need to maintain state
FOLLOW_PATTERN = Use Strategy pattern when implementing different algorithms or behaviors

// Naming Conventions
CONVENTION = Suffix test classes with "Test" (e.g., AccountServiceTest)
CONVENTION = Use "Interface" Suffix for interfaces (e.g., TriggerHandlerInterface)
CONVENTION = Use "Batch" Suffix for Batches (e.g., AccountBatch)
CONVENTION = Use "Schedule" Suffix for Schedules (e.g., AccountSchedule)
CONVENTION = Use "Queueable" suffix for Queueable implementations (e.g., AccountProcessQueueable)
CONVENTION = Use "Utility" or "Utils" suffix for utility classes (e.g., DateUtils)